          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/lab-Grown-diamond-jewelry-guide-1.jpg",
            "image_position": "right",
            "title": "What is a lab-grown diamond?",
            "title_url": "",
            "description": "<p>As their name suggests, lab-grown diamonds are diamonds which are created in a laboratory instead of being mined.</p><p>Essentially, scientists are able to replicate in a lab the natural process that results in the creation of diamonds. While mined diamonds take millions of years to be created, scientists can create diamonds in a lab in a fraction of that time. It actually just takes about two months for them to grow. Impressive, right?</p><p>But the best thing about lab-grown diamonds is that they’re as much more sustainable, ethical, and accessible than their mined counterpart. Lab-grown diamonds are the epitome of ecological and accessible luxury.</p>",
            "content_width": 50
          }
        },
        "item_4GdjVN": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/lab-Grown-diamond-jewelry-guide-2.jpg",
            "image_position": "left",
            "title": "Are lab-grown diamonds real?",
            "title_url": "",
            "description": "<p>As their name suggests, lab-grown diamonds are diamonds which are created in a laboratory instead of being mined.</p><p>Essentially, scientists are able to replicate in a lab the natural process that results in the creation of diamonds. While mined diamonds take millions of years to be created, scientists can create diamonds in a lab in a fraction of that time. It actually just takes about two months for them to grow. Impressive, right?</p><p>But the best thing about lab-grown diamonds is that they’re as much more sustainable, ethical, and accessible than their mined counterpart. Lab-grown diamonds are the epitome of ecological and accessible luxury.</p>",
            "content_width": 50
          }
        },
        "item_f3BcGq": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/lab-Grown-diamond-jewelry-guide-3.jpg",
            "image_position": "right",
            "title": "How are lab-grown diamonds made?",
            "title_url": "",
            "description": "<p>The process of growing diamonds in a lab involves cutting-edge equipment, carbon, huge amounts of pressure, and extremely high temperatures, all in a controlled environment.</p><p>Labs use two different methods to grow diamonds: High Pressure-High Temperature (HPHT) and Chemical Vapor Deposition (CVD). They’re both incredibly complex, but here’s the gist: a so-called \"diamond seed\" is placed inside a sealed chamber where that carbon seed is pressurized and heated until its little particles break down and crystallize into a fully formed diamond.</p><p>That might seem like a weird process, but that’s exactly what happens in nature, too. The difference is that nature takes millions of years to grow diamonds, while we can do it in a matter of months. It’s pretty amazing!</p>",
            "content_width": 50
          }
        },
        "item_MByMT9": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/lab-Grown-diamond-jewelry-guide-4.jpg",
            "image_position": "left",
            "title": "Can you tell the difference between lab-grown diamonds and mined diamonds?",
            "title_url": "",
            "description": "<p>Both lab-grown and mined diamonds have the same identical chemical composition and structure, and you can’t tell them apart without using professional equipment.</p><p>Distinguishing between the two requires a trained gemologist and specific equipment designed to identify lab-grown diamonds.</p><p>That’s what’s so great about it: both diamonds have an equal play of light and luster, hardness, refraction, and density. It’s easy to see why they’re so hard to resist.</p>",
            "content_width": 50
          }
        }
      },
